cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hermes-rubric in your research, please cite it."
title: "hermes-rubric: Evidence-first structured scoring for LLM-judged artifacts"
abstract: >-
  hermes-rubric is an evidence-first scoring scaffold for LLM-as-judge
  evaluation. It enforces a three-stage pipeline (rubric synthesis,
  per-dimension evidence collection, evidence-only scoring) so that the
  resulting score has an audit trail. Class-aware rubric templates
  (v1.0) determinize Stage-1, producing fixed dim sets across runs.
  Cross-model Cohen's κ = 0.629 across 96 paired runs on the
  batch-equivalence test set.
